potemnevshiy-pergament-name = darkened parchment
potemnevshiy-pergament-desc = A dense sheet of paper with uneven edges and a hard, sweeping hand. The lower half of the parchment is heavily soaked with something brown, warping the paper and making the final lines almost impossible to read.
potemnevshiy-pergament-content = [head=2]FORTRESS ORDER[/head]


    {"For everyone whose high ideals of liberty have finally blown out of their skulls and made room for ordinary greed."}


    {"Yesterday, beyond the northern wall, a certain Bertram of the third ten was intercepted. This unrecognized genius of diplomacy carried a detailed chart of our posts and the night watch schedule. Apparently the boy decided the Legate in Port would generously pour Imperial silver into his hands for such touching concern for legionary health."}


    {"As a lesson to all other lovers of double games:"}


    {"[bullet] Hang the aforementioned Bertram in the square by the gate immediately."}

    {"[bullet] Do not remove the boots or jacket from the deceased. Let him hang in full dress until the rope rots and the ravens leave nothing of him but bones."}


    {"Anyone who decides our secrets can be so easily converted into ringing coin will have his ribs counted by me personally. The Empire is far away, but my noose is right here, above your stupid [color=#8b0000]▓▓▓▒▒[/color]"}


    {"And if I learn that anyone from [color=#8b0000]████▓▓[/color] helped him carry out [color=#5c4033]▓▓▒▒░[/color]"}

    {"[color=#8b0000]██████▓▓▒▒[/color] will be dangling from the next [color=#8b0000]██▓▓▒[/color]"}

    {"[color=#5c4033]████████▓▓▓▒▒▒░░░[/color]"}

    {"[color=#5c4033]████████████▓▓▓▓▒▒▒▒░░[/color]"}

potrepannaya-zapiska-name = battered note
potrepannaya-zapiska-desc = A small scrap of cheap, slightly damp paper. The handwriting is crooked, the letters jumping every which way, as though written in great haste or with a hangover. The sheet clearly reeks of sour cabbage and foul tobacco.
potrepannaya-zapiska-content = [head=2]Reminder for a bungler[/head]


    {"Listen here, [bolditalic]Ryaboy[/bolditalic]. I have gone to stand watch on the eastern wall. By the time I return, everything on this list had better be done, or you will sleep in the nearest bush:"}


    {"[bullet] [bold]Fix the roof![/bold] Last night so much water dripped down my collar that I could have raised trout in it. Take moss from the palisade and plug the hole above my bunk."}

    {"[bullet] [bold]Go to Foring.[/bold] Take him those wolf pelts. Trade them for [color=tan]proper groats[/color], not the moldy dust he shoved on us last time."}

    {"[bullet] [bold]The hearth.[/bold] Chop dry wood and keep the fire going. The draft here is icy."}


    {"And just try spending our last coins on dice again! [color=#8b0000]I will break your fingers one by one with a hammer.[/color]"}


    {"Your elder brother, [italic]Gunther[/italic]"}

zakopchennyy-pergament-name = soot-blackened parchment
zakopchennyy-pergament-desc = A rough, dense sheet of paper smelling of smoke and scale. The text is written with such furious pressure that the stiff quill nearly tore through the parchment in places.
zakopchennyy-pergament-content = [head=2]LISTEN HERE, IDLERS![/head]


    {"If one more snot-nosed fool brings me a bent Imperial spear and asks me to reforge it into an \"elegant blade\", I will shove that shaft flatwise up his backside!"}


    {"I am a blacksmith, not a miracle worker. You cannot forge an elven saber from a rusty piece of shit, even if Foring gives me a mountain of the best coal. Your weapons must punch through legionary armor, not sparkle prettily in the sun!"}


    {"So understand this once and for all:"}

    {"[bullet] Bring scrap only after cleaning off swamp slime and dried blood! My forge is not a slaughterhouse. The stink cuts the eyes."}

    {"[bullet] Stop whining that shields are heavy and swords drag toward the ground. Eat more porridge, sons of dogs, and train your arms! In battle, the Legate will not give discounts for dead muscle."}

    {"[bullet] Whoever takes my tongs to crack nuts again will lose his fingers."}


    {"Now march to the walls before I straighten someone's spine with a hammer!"}

akkuratnye-zapisi-name = neat notes
akkuratnye-zapisi-desc = A yellowed sheet of thick parchment with uneven edges. The text is written in flawless calligraphy with a distinctive slant. The document gives off a faint scent of sandalwood and bitter almond mixed with the smell of old ink.
akkuratnye-zapisi-content = [head=3]Personal Notes[/head]


    {"Fools believe Fort Rebellion stands on their ridiculous ideals, pompous speeches, and the Jarl's valor. Charming naivety. War stands on gold and timely supplies. And on me."}


    {"Take these port craftsmen, for instance. Tearful nonentities never stop writing complaints about Roger Palmer. They are offended to the depths of their souls that the bone blacksmith works day and night without tiring and pulls red-hot cannonballs from the forge with his bare hands. They whine about \"fair competition\" while I buy choice steel from Palmer for coppers. He has not a drop of the living laziness and pride found in the rest. Perhaps he is the only man in this port whose silence and productivity deserve my respect."}


    {"The same cannot be said of our quartermaster. An entirely different sort of disappointment. He robs his own army with such confidence that one might think he personally invented corruption. I buy state salt pork from him for almost nothing purely for the pleasure of watching him sweat and flick his eyes about at each of our meetings."}


    {"Vsevolod sincerely believes his schemes are a great secret. Naive coward. Tomorrow my \"confidentiality fee\" doubles. Let him squirm. I hate miserly men, and he manages also to be pathetic with remarkable elegance."}


    {"- Aurelia ex Inferis"}

donesenie-yarlu-name = report to the Jarl
donesenie-yarlu-content = [head=3]To His Grace the Jarl[/head]


    {"I am forced to tear you away from blueprints and global strategy. Leave heroic epics to the bards, Jarl. My men are ready to hold this cursed line against the Legion until the second coming, but there is one nuance: we are losing the war not under enemy cannonballs, but in accounting books."}


    {"I speak of our priceless quartermaster. Vsevolod Volkhovsky has revealed a truly outstanding talent for logistical alchemy. Any convoy of supplies leaving the gates of your citadel shrinks exactly by half on its way to the front. Last week this financial genius sent us ten kegs of powder instead of twenty, and the powder was so damp it would be safer to season porridge with it than load cannon. As for the porridge itself, I shall tactfully remain silent. Volkhovsky's ability to sell proper salt pork to port hucksters and feed blatant rot to the front requires a certain business acumen."}


    {"I would take the greatest pleasure in visiting this enterprising bastard personally and conducting an audit with a rope and the nearest branch. Alas, our hero prefers to show miracles of courage by sitting behind the thick walls of the main fortress, where my authority, to my deepest regret, does not reach."}


    {"Therefore I propose a simple administrative solution. Walk to the quartermaster stores. And if you do not want my garrison to die of exhaustion and dysentery before enemy galleys even appear on the horizon, hang Volkhovsky in the inner yard. For all my boundless respect, I am a poor necromancer and have not yet learned to command corpses."}

staraya-listovka-name = old leaflet
staraya-listovka-desc = An official appeal of the Inquisition of Hellfire to respectable layfolk.
staraya-listovka-content = [head=3]Vigilance is the shield of our world![/head]


    {"Brothers and sisters! Today we see those who were recently driven off with red-hot iron walking ever more freely through the streets of our settlements. Inferns. We are told that through fire and blood they won their right to exist after the last war. We are urged toward peace with the horned folk."}


    {"But the Inquisition does not forget the past and calls upon you not to lose vigilance!"}


    {"Do not be deceived by their feigned calm. Remember the deeds for which they were persecuted since time immemorial. All honest races know the truth: their frightening appearance reflects their essence. While we strive with all our strength to hold the Barrier and save this world from darkness, to whom do they secretly bow? Their idols are Pyrx and Kreza. Their hidden tongue is the Ancient language, spoken by no good people."}


    {"They have learned the Common tongue, wear ordinary clothing, and take the same work as you. But their nature is unchanged. Behind their false civility lie savage customs, and behind a merchant's smile, readiness to seize the throat at any moment."}


    {"The Church sternly warns:"}

    {"1. Do not admit inferns into your homes and do not make deals with them. Their gold is soaked in blood."}

    {"2. Watch their gatherings closely. If you hear their guttural whispers in the Ancient language, know that new treason is ripening."}

    {"3. Drive them away from artifacts and magical nodes. They care nothing for maintaining the Barrier."}


    {"They tore by force the right to breathe the same air as us, but they will never earn our trust. Keep a sober mind, keep steel ready, and report any suspicious step they take!"}

pismo-dzhonu-name = Letter to John
pismo-dzhonu-content = John, you old stump!


    {"I bow to you through this scrap of parchment. I am sitting in the Lame Fox, and the beer here is sour swill. Without your mug, drinking is no joy at all. Remember last winter, when we argued who could chop through the bootleg of the frozen innkeeper faster? Ah, you merry bastard..."}


    {"I will send you a sharpened axe. Yours must be dull from stumps on the northern edge. Just do not poke into that old adit beyond the ravine. The locals found a crawlway there, and it smells not of mushrooms but of something sweet that makes the beasts scatter. I know your stupid habit of dragging home everything that shines in the dark."}


    {"Guard your neck. And come to the fair in two weeks. My Molly bakes a tripe pie that would make even a dead man sneeze."}


    {"Your friend,"}

    {"Thomas the Smith"}


    {"P.S. You still never told me why you begged that long nail off me. If you drive it into your boot, do not expect me to dig you out. If you hear a whisper underground calling you by name, run. And if you do not run... well, then farewell, old friend."}

pomyatyy-pergament02-name = crumpled parchment
pomyatyy-pergament02-desc = A dense sheet of paper, the text written in a broad, firm hand, the letters formed with cold calculation and not a single unnecessary flourish. In places the ink has blurred slightly from damp.
pomyatyy-pergament02-content = [head=2]Directive[/head]


    {"Gentlemen half-slaughtered fighters for freedom. It has come to my attention that our noble struggle against the Emperor's tyranny is swiftly degenerating into an ordinary tavern."}


    {"Yesterday patrolmen somehow dragged a keg of foul swill into the barracks, calmly trading it for bundles of our own crossbow bolts. What do you intend to shoot with when the Legate deigns to bring his chained dogs out of Port? Empty mugs and lofty speeches about liberty? [color=#4a4a4a]▓▓▓[/color]"}


    {"I do not need a crowd of drunken idiots on the walls. The Legion will not wait for you to sober up and remember which end of a spear to hold. Therefore:"}


    {"[bullet] All surplus provisions, iron, and warm clothing are henceforth turned over to Foring. In person and on record. No improvisation. [color=#2b2b2b]▒▒▒[/color]"}

    {"[bullet] Watches on the southern side are doubled. If I or my trusted people find a sentry asleep at his post, he will clean the fortress latrine pits for the rest of his days. Which, I assure you, will arrive very soon."}


    {"If anyone thinks rebellion is an excuse to stuff himself without consequence and spit on discipline, you have entered the wrong door. We are surviving here, not celebrating."}

zalyapannaya-chelobitnaya-name = stained petition
zalyapannaya-chelobitnaya-desc = A crumpled piece of paper thickly stained with beer, soot, and grease. The writing is crooked, apparently taken down by a scribe for a couple of coppers from the words of a half-drunk crowd.
zalyapannaya-chelobitnaya-content = [head=3]Petition to the bright Jarl from the port craftsmen[/head]


    {"Bright Lord Jarl, our chief and protector!"}


    {"We bow low, honest blacksmiths and hammermen of the port, and tearfully beg your mercy! Save us from ruin, good lord, for our human strength is no more! There has appeared here in the port, if one may say so, accursed undead. Calls himself Roger Palmer. And if only he howled by night in the graveyard, but no, the son of a bitch opened a forge!"}


    {"How, tell us by mercy, are we to compete with that bag of bones? We are living men! We must fill our bellies, gulp ale to wet our throats from soot, and sleep at least a little. But that bone pest needs neither food, nor sleep, nor, gods forgive, a run to the privy! He stands by the forge day and night, rattling his bones, riveting cannon for the Legion and anchors for our galleys so hard that sparks fly to the sky!"}


    {"The other day our Mikula saw with his own eyes how that Roger pulled a red-hot cannonball straight out of the coals with his bare bony claws! It is not hot to him, damn it, nor painful! He just wipes his bare skull with a rag, grins his teeth, and goes back to swinging the hammer like a demon in the underworld."}


    {"The bastard cuts prices so low we may as well take begging sacks and walk the world. Our quartermasters now haul every contract to him, because a skeleton need not be paid in bread, so he takes coppers. Soon we will be eating rotten tripe from hunger, and our wives with little children will leap into the ocean from the cliffs for such a life!"}


    {"Have mercy, most bright benefactor! Rein in that Palmer! Order some horse-sized tax laid on him for not buying food, or make him close his forge at night so things are like they are for honest folk! Otherwise we will take that skeleton apart bone by bone and feed him to stray dogs, by God!"}


    {"We place crosses instead of signatures:"}

    {"Mikula X,"}

    {"Ryaboy X,"}

    {"Klim One-Ear x"}

    {"and another dozen artel men."}

rvanyy-pergament-name = torn parchment
rvanyy-pergament-desc = Verses of a disappointed rower.
rvanyy-pergament-content = Ah, ocean, boundless rolling swell!

    {"All my life I dreamed of you well."}

    {"I left my home and joined the fleet,"}

    {"Thought some mermaid I would meet."}


    {"But on the galley there is sweat,"}

    {"Sour cabbage, old boots wet."}

    {"Sergeant yells, the gunner spews,"}

    {"And gruel bowls drift into view."}


    {"They told me: \"Cannons are our pride!\""}

    {"And I must scrub their muzzles wide."}

    {"Instead of treasure, coin, and fame,"}

    {"One rotten hardtack is my claim."}


    {"To hell with romance, ropes, and mast!"}

    {"Sea passions can kiss my past."}

    {"Once we set foot upon the quay,"}

    {"I will join Ipat's staff, you'll see!"}

